<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tepantitla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tepantitla is an apartment compound at Teotihuacan, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyramid-of-the-sun">Pyramid of the Sun</a>, famous for its well-preserved murals. Its paintings show a storm god or goddess with priests and a lively scene of small figures playing, swimming and singing in a watery landscape, often called the Tlalocan mural. They are among the finest examples of Teotihuacan painting.</p></div>
